{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDKkubcHitkqmJaLXcd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so the shares add back up to the full 1 zł.\n\n**What was wrong:** in `money.py`, `split_cents` used floor division (`total // people`) and threw away the remainder.\n\n**Fix:** it now uses `divmod` to get the even share and the leftover grosze, then gives one extra grosz to each of the first few people until the leftover is used up. No two people's shares ever differ by more than 1 grosz.\n\n**Tests:** I added two tests to `test_money.py` and checked that both failed before the fix:\n- `split_cents(100, 3) == [34, 33, 33]`\n- A wider check over many totals and group sizes: the shares always add up to the total, and the largest and smallest share differ by at most 1.\n\nAll 5 tests now pass with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\nThe first people in the list always get the extra grosz. If you'd rather spread that around (for example, rotate who pays it), that's a quick change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":539,"cache_read_input_tokens":19227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":539},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b2cfe7e-556d-452f-8965-6687edaefb14","uuid":"f21c9c5d-1fd7-417d-a488-e5d092849486","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:14:44.085Z","request_id":"req_011CggDKkfxNAwZKyoaG1vtN"}
